{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25146406",
      "title": "How Does Authentication Work (In React & NextJS Apps)?",
      "lectureOrder": 395,
      "videoOrder": 364,
      "sourceHash": "c1d1b130f72877c6a3f401e7b7ad57045447ce2af358be8a9f521fb4118f339a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.15,
          "end": 6.32,
          "en": "So how does authentication work in general?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.32,
          "end": 8.98,
          "en": "And then also specifically in React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.98,
          "end": 11.363,
          "en": "and the Next.js applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.5,
          "end": 15.62,
          "en": "The core idea is always the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.62,
          "end": 17.01,
          "en": "We have our client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.01,
          "end": 20.64,
          "en": "so our browser and the user visiting our page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.64,
          "end": 25.24,
          "en": "through that browser and our server serving that page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.24,
          "end": 28.43,
          "en": "The server also is connected to a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.43,
          "end": 33.17,
          "en": "where for example, all our registered users are stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.17,
          "end": 36.66,
          "en": "Now let's assume a user did already create an account.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.66,
          "end": 41.59,
          "en": "And now that same user visits our page and wants to log in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.59,
          "end": 43.02,
          "en": "How does that work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.02,
          "end": 47.12,
          "en": "Well, the user enters some data into a login form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.12,
          "end": 50.22,
          "en": "like this form here for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.22,
          "end": 51.46,
          "en": "in the log-in mode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.46,
          "end": 55.74,
          "en": "So the user enters some data here and clicks log in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.74,
          "end": 56.94,
          "en": "When that happens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.94,
          "end": 60.91,
          "en": "we send the request with JavaScript to the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.91,
          "end": 63.57,
          "en": "our request which contains the user data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.57,
          "end": 66.24,
          "en": "email and password for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.24,
          "end": 70.4,
          "en": "then on the server, we can validate that input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.4,
          "end": 72.72,
          "en": "We can reach out to our database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.72,
          "end": 76.85,
          "en": "and see if we find an account for that email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.85,
          "end": 79.89,
          "en": "And if the entered password matches the password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.89,
          "end": 81.77,
          "en": "we find in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.77,
          "end": 83.64,
          "en": "And then we sent back a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.64,
          "end": 87.85,
          "en": "which basically says, yes, your credentials were correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.85,
          "end": 89.38,
          "en": "You are authenticated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.38,
          "end": 93.89,
          "en": "or which declines the authentication request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.89,
          "end": 98.33,
          "en": "And then once we sent back that yes or no response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.33,
          "end": 99.69,
          "en": "though it's a bit more than that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.69,
          "end": 101.1,
          "en": "as you will see in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.1,
          "end": 103.62,
          "en": "But once you send it back that response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.62,
          "end": 108.38,
          "en": "the client can there after also reach protected routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.38,
          "end": 111.82,
          "en": "and send requests to other endpoints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.82,
          "end": 116.82,
          "en": "on our server to our URLs on our server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.9,
          "end": 119.81,
          "en": "that might require authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.81,
          "end": 122.22,
          "en": "Like for example that profile page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.22,
          "end": 125.96,
          "en": "We're only able to reach it once we are authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.96,
          "end": 130.96,
          "en": "And we also only can change the password if we are.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.15,
          "end": 135.013,
          "en": "So if that request is sent to some backend API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.013,
          "end": 138.96,
          "en": "that the old password should be replaced with a new one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.96,
          "end": 143,
          "en": "that kind of request should only be allowed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143,
          "end": 147.29,
          "en": "and fulfilled if the user is authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.29,
          "end": 149.5,
          "en": "So that request which we send here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.5,
          "end": 152.87,
          "en": "needs some extra data attached to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.87,
          "end": 155.74,
          "en": "some extra data attached to the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.74,
          "end": 158.23,
          "en": "which in the end tells the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.23,
          "end": 160.85,
          "en": "that this user is authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.85,
          "end": 164.81,
          "en": "Because anyone could be sending requests to our API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.81,
          "end": 169.28,
          "en": "and hence the request needs to carry some extra permission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.28,
          "end": 172.61,
          "en": "which then should be verified on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.61,
          "end": 175.2,
          "en": "And that permission part is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.2,
          "end": 178.69,
          "en": "Because a simple yes or no sent back by the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.69,
          "end": 181.51,
          "en": "to the client would not be enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.51,
          "end": 185.34,
          "en": "Because we can of course always send a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.34,
          "end": 189.05,
          "en": "to some API and point that requires authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.05,
          "end": 191.78,
          "en": "and say, \"Hey, I'm authenticated.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.78,
          "end": 196.32,
          "en": "We can't just believe that as the author of the API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.32,
          "end": 200.27,
          "en": "we need some proof that a user is authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.27,
          "end": 202.82,
          "en": "And therefore authentication involves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.82,
          "end": 206.4,
          "en": "this exchange of credentials for permission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 206.4,
          "end": 208.06,
          "en": "But the permission is more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 208.06,
          "end": 210,
          "en": "than just a yes or no.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210,
          "end": 212.61,
          "en": "To be precise we can't just save",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.61,
          "end": 214.72,
          "en": "and use a simple yes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.72,
          "end": 217.38,
          "en": "because of fake yes, could be sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.38,
          "end": 220.57,
          "en": "We can't just tell our server that we are authenticated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.57,
          "end": 223.03,
          "en": "and then request protected data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 223.03,
          "end": 225.98,
          "en": "or perform protected operations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 225.98,
          "end": 228.56,
          "en": "And therefore, instead we need some proof.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.56,
          "end": 231.62,
          "en": "Some proof which con to be faked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 231.62,
          "end": 234.55,
          "en": "And for this, we've got two main mechanisms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.55,
          "end": 239.55,
          "en": "We got server-side sessions and authentication tokens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.72,
          "end": 242.27,
          "en": "Now these are two common approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.27,
          "end": 246.97,
          "en": "for solving this problem of unfakable permissions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.97,
          "end": 250.13,
          "en": "The concept of server-side sessions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.13,
          "end": 255.13,
          "en": "works such that we store some unique identifier on a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 255.93,
          "end": 260.55,
          "en": "So we generate some session ID, which is unique.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 260.55,
          "end": 262.79,
          "en": "And we store that on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.79,
          "end": 264.85,
          "en": "for example, in a database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264.85,
          "end": 268.64,
          "en": "And we sent that same identifier to the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.64,
          "end": 270.95,
          "en": "that sent us the credentials.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.95,
          "end": 275.95,
          "en": "Then on the client, we can store that ID that identifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 277.02,
          "end": 279.3,
          "en": "And then we can use that stored identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.3,
          "end": 283.09000000000003,
          "en": "to attach it to requests which we there after are send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 283.09000000000003,
          "end": 286.28,
          "en": "to protected resources on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 286.28,
          "end": 289.58,
          "en": "And then the server is always able to extract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.58,
          "end": 292.75,
          "en": "that identifier from the incoming requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.75,
          "end": 296.37,
          "en": "check if it's stored that identifier in the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 296.37,
          "end": 299,
          "en": "and if it did grant access,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 299,
          "end": 302.21,
          "en": "and if it does not deny access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 302.21,
          "end": 303.75,
          "en": "Now then only clients",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 303.75,
          "end": 307.176,
          "en": "which have does identifier are able to send requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 307.176,
          "end": 311.72,
          "en": "Now you might say, okay, but can this identify be stolen?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 311.72,
          "end": 314.79,
          "en": "Well, whilst it's in transit it shouldn't be stolen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 314.79,
          "end": 317.04,
          "en": "because we should be using SSL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 317.04,
          "end": 319.94,
          "en": "for encrypting to connection anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 319.94,
          "end": 322.96,
          "en": "And when it is stored on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 322.96,
          "end": 325.32,
          "en": "it is stored in a cookie typically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 325.32,
          "end": 327.29,
          "en": "and that cookie can be configured",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 327.29,
          "end": 331.03,
          "en": "such that it's not accessible through JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 331.03,
          "end": 334.08,
          "en": "to prevent against cross-site scripting attacks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 334.08,
          "end": 337.74,
          "en": "And that it is only readable from the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 337.74,
          "end": 341.04,
          "en": "when it is attached to outgoing requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 341.04,
          "end": 344.56,
          "en": "And even if it would be accessible through JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 344.56,
          "end": 345.83,
          "en": "you should be protecting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 345.83,
          "end": 349.3,
          "en": "against cross-site scripting attacks anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 349.3,
          "end": 352.69,
          "en": "And if you can rule out cross-site scripting attacks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 352.69,
          "end": 356.01,
          "en": "your authentication permission stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 356.01,
          "end": 359.18,
          "en": "in some client-side storage is pretty secure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 359.18,
          "end": 362.26,
          "en": "Because only you, the owner of this computer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 362.26,
          "end": 365.26,
          "en": "and the user of this browser are able to view it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 365.26,
          "end": 368.23,
          "en": "So you could only hack yourself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 368.23,
          "end": 371.73,
          "en": "and some random dude wouldn't be able to just send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 371.73,
          "end": 373.72,
          "en": "a fake request to the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 373.72,
          "end": 377.07,
          "en": "because whilst you could come up with a random identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 377.07,
          "end": 380.71,
          "en": "the server would not know that identifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 380.71,
          "end": 383.63,
          "en": "So that's the concept of server-side sessions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 383.63,
          "end": 386.97,
          "en": "The other concept is about authentication tokens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 386.97,
          "end": 389.08,
          "en": "It's not that far off.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 389.08,
          "end": 392.76,
          "en": "The idea here is that the server does not store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 392.76,
          "end": 394.40999999999997,
          "en": "any identifiers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 394.40999999999997,
          "end": 398.61,
          "en": "Instead, the server creates and signs tokens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 398.61,
          "end": 402.31,
          "en": "Which in the end are just a random strings you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 402.31,
          "end": 407.31,
          "en": "Random strings which can be unpacked to data packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 408.15999999999997,
          "end": 410.03,
          "en": "so we take various pieces of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 410.03,
          "end": 412.71,
          "en": "and sign them together more on that in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 412.71,
          "end": 416.3,
          "en": "And then such a token is sent back to the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 416.3,
          "end": 418.47,
          "en": "The client can then save that token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 418.47,
          "end": 421.27,
          "en": "and again attach it to outgoing requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 421.27,
          "end": 424.72,
          "en": "to tell the server that access should be granted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 424.72,
          "end": 427.91,
          "en": "Now, even though the server does not store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 427.91,
          "end": 431.2,
          "en": "that token in a database or anywhere else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 431.2,
          "end": 434.82,
          "en": "the server knows how it's signed that token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 434.82,
          "end": 437.08,
          "en": "And I'll come back to that in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 437.08,
          "end": 439.93,
          "en": "So the server will be able to verify",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 439.93,
          "end": 443.6,
          "en": "if a token was created by it or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 443.6,
          "end": 446.65,
          "en": "And therefore, again if I just come up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 446.65,
          "end": 448.93,
          "en": "with some random token string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 448.93,
          "end": 451.75,
          "en": "and I send this to a server to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 451.75,
          "end": 455.52,
          "en": "to some protected resource access would be denied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 455.52,
          "end": 457.77,
          "en": "because the server would not be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 457.77,
          "end": 460.14,
          "en": "to verify my random string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 460.14,
          "end": 463.3,
          "en": "Because it wouldn't be a validly signed token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 463.3,
          "end": 465.64,
          "en": "generated by that server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 465.64,
          "end": 468.55,
          "en": "Now these are the two approaches we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 468.55,
          "end": 471.61,
          "en": "Now when we build a single-page application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 471.61,
          "end": 475.39,
          "en": "which we in the end still kind of do with Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 475.39,
          "end": 479.11,
          "en": "then we typically work with tokens instead of sessions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 479.11,
          "end": 481.41,
          "en": "And there are reasons for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 481.41,
          "end": 484.71,
          "en": "For one, pages are served directly and populated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 484.71,
          "end": 488.97,
          "en": "with logic without necessarily hitting the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 488.97,
          "end": 491.64,
          "en": "Of course, when working with Next.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 491.64,
          "end": 493.52,
          "en": "you can build pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 493.52,
          "end": 496.4,
          "en": "which use get server-side props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 496.4,
          "end": 499.08,
          "en": "and therefore there will be a request handled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 499.08,
          "end": 502.53,
          "en": "by the server every time that page is being served.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 502.53,
          "end": 506.16,
          "en": "But you will also have many pages which are pre-generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 506.16,
          "end": 508.86,
          "en": "And once the user is on your website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 508.86,
          "end": 513.1,
          "en": "many pages won't be fetched from the backend at all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 513.1,
          "end": 514.69,
          "en": "but instead will be loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 514.69,
          "end": 519.59,
          "en": "and generated dynamically with front-end JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 519.59,
          "end": 522.72,
          "en": "because you still have a single-page application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 522.72,
          "end": 526.3,
          "en": "at least for many pages that make up your website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 526.3,
          "end": 529.24,
          "en": "after you initially loaded your first page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 529.24,
          "end": 531.95,
          "en": "then still JavaScript takes over,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 531.95,
          "end": 536.07,
          "en": "React takes over and handles your website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 536.07,
          "end": 537.41,
          "en": "So that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 537.41,
          "end": 540.63,
          "en": "You don't send a request for every page you visit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 540.63,
          "end": 543.49,
          "en": "because you're not using get server-side props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 543.49,
          "end": 544.99,
          "en": "on every page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 544.99,
          "end": 548.66,
          "en": "So to server, doesn't see every request which you send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 548.66,
          "end": 551.13,
          "en": "and therefore you load pages without the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 551.13,
          "end": 553.66,
          "en": "being able to directly find out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 553.66,
          "end": 556.09,
          "en": "if you are authenticated or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 556.09,
          "end": 559.26,
          "en": "In addition, backend APIs which be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 559.26,
          "end": 563.01,
          "en": "for a single-page applications are typically stateless.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 563.01,
          "end": 566.85,
          "en": "They don't care about the individual connected clients.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 566.85,
          "end": 570.21,
          "en": "They don't keep track of all the connected clients.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 570.21,
          "end": 572.02,
          "en": "Instead, the idea is that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 572.02,
          "end": 575.74,
          "en": "that API can work pretty much on its own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 575.74,
          "end": 578.7,
          "en": "And it just is able to hand out permissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 578.7,
          "end": 581.81,
          "en": "to clients who authenticated so that they can then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 581.81,
          "end": 585.42,
          "en": "later request access to protect the resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 585.42,
          "end": 589.52,
          "en": "The API itself does not store any extra information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 589.52,
          "end": 592.3,
          "en": "about any connected clients.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 592.3,
          "end": 595.84,
          "en": "And since this is how we build single-page applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 595.84,
          "end": 599.71,
          "en": "the server is not involved in every request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 599.71,
          "end": 602.9,
          "en": "and every action that's happening on our page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 602.9,
          "end": 606.16,
          "en": "because we handled that with front-end JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 606.16,
          "end": 610.62,
          "en": "and we have that stateless API connected to the SPA.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 610.62,
          "end": 611.95,
          "en": "And because of all of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 611.95,
          "end": 615.64,
          "en": "we could say that we have kind of a detached front-end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 615.64,
          "end": 617.51,
          "en": "and back-end combination.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 617.51,
          "end": 620.09,
          "en": "They do talk to each other sometimes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 620.09,
          "end": 624.1,
          "en": "but not for every action that's going on on the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 624.1,
          "end": 627.66,
          "en": "And because that's the case, servers don't save information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 627.66,
          "end": 629.56,
          "en": "about authenticated clients.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 629.56,
          "end": 633.36,
          "en": "And instead clients should get that standalone permission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 633.36,
          "end": 637.08,
          "en": "which allows them to prove that they are authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 637.08,
          "end": 639.66,
          "en": "And that's why we use these tokens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 639.66,
          "end": 640.93,
          "en": "And here specifically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 640.93,
          "end": 644.21,
          "en": "we use a concept called JSON Web Tokens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 644.21,
          "end": 646.2,
          "en": "that is simply the most common form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 646.2,
          "end": 648.36,
          "en": "of authentication token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 648.36,
          "end": 651.38,
          "en": "And it's simply describes the way the token is generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 651.38,
          "end": 654.51,
          "en": "though we don't need to care about that too much",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 654.51,
          "end": 657.78,
          "en": "because we'll use a third-party library for generating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 657.78,
          "end": 659.993,
          "en": "and signing that token anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 660.93,
          "end": 664.74,
          "en": "So as it seems, these JSON Web Tokens are important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 212,
          "start": 664.74,
          "end": 666.853,
          "en": "and therefore we should take a closer look at them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 213,
          "start": 666.853,
          "end": 671.13,
          "en": "We should understand how exactly JSON Web Tokens work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 214,
          "start": 671.13,
          "end": 672.79,
          "en": "And in the end that JSON Web Tokens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 215,
          "start": 672.79,
          "end": 677.723,
          "en": "is generated with three main blocks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 216,
          "start": 678.56,
          "end": 680.7,
          "en": "We got some issuer data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 217,
          "start": 680.7,
          "end": 684.04,
          "en": "Some data which is automatically added into a token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 218,
          "start": 684.04,
          "end": 687.53,
          "en": "by the server when that token is generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 219,
          "start": 687.53,
          "end": 690.4,
          "en": "That's some metadata which we typically don't set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 220,
          "start": 690.4,
          "end": 692.26,
          "en": "ourselves as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 221,
          "start": 692.26,
          "end": 695.95,
          "en": "but which is pre-configured by the third party packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 222,
          "start": 695.95,
          "end": 698.54,
          "en": "we use for generating tokens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 223,
          "start": 698.54,
          "end": 702.68,
          "en": "We can then still also add custom data to our token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 224,
          "start": 702.68,
          "end": 705.26,
          "en": "for example, some information about the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 225,
          "start": 706.13,
          "end": 707.93,
          "en": "and then very important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 226,
          "start": 707.93,
          "end": 710.49,
          "en": "we also set up a secret key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 227,
          "start": 710.49,
          "end": 713.6,
          "en": "We set up that key on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 228,
          "start": 713.6,
          "end": 716.7,
          "en": "The client never gets to see that key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 229,
          "start": 716.7,
          "end": 719.9,
          "en": "And that's important because if you have that key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 230,
          "start": 719.9,
          "end": 722.55,
          "en": "you can create valid tokens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 231,
          "start": 722.55,
          "end": 724.74,
          "en": "which are accepted by the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 232,
          "start": 724.74,
          "end": 728.12,
          "en": "Hence only the server knows that key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 233,
          "start": 728.12,
          "end": 732.53,
          "en": "Then we generate a token with some third-party package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 234,
          "start": 732.53,
          "end": 734.86,
          "en": "by combining all these pieces together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 235,
          "start": 734.86,
          "end": 739.69,
          "en": "by creating a random string that incorporates all that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 236,
          "start": 739.69,
          "end": 741.66,
          "en": "and is signed by that key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 237,
          "start": 741.66,
          "end": 743.98,
          "en": "And that is that JSON Web Token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 238,
          "start": 743.98,
          "end": 745.373,
          "en": "a long string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 239,
          "start": 746.22,
          "end": 748.01,
          "en": "The important thing here is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 240,
          "start": 748.01,
          "end": 750.84,
          "en": "signing does not mean encryption.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 241,
          "start": 750.84,
          "end": 754.02,
          "en": "The JSON Web Token is not encrypted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 242,
          "start": 754.02,
          "end": 757.72,
          "en": "You can unpack it and read the data inside of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 243,
          "start": 757.72,
          "end": 759.81,
          "en": "without knowing that key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 244,
          "start": 759.81,
          "end": 764.81,
          "en": "That key only proves that a given server created that token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 245,
          "start": 765.71,
          "end": 768.01,
          "en": "But you can read the content of the token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 246,
          "start": 768.01,
          "end": 769.64,
          "en": "without knowing that key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 247,
          "start": 769.64,
          "end": 773.04,
          "en": "The key of course will not be included in the token though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 248,
          "start": 773.04,
          "end": 775.02,
          "en": "So you can't read that key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 249,
          "start": 775.02,
          "end": 777.733,
          "en": "even if you unpack the token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 250,
          "start": 779.39,
          "end": 782.61,
          "en": "Now is that token which then is stored by the client?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 251,
          "start": 782.61,
          "end": 783.84,
          "en": "Sorry. By the browser?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 252,
          "start": 783.84,
          "end": 785.34,
          "en": "And which then is attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 253,
          "start": 785.34,
          "end": 789.72,
          "en": "to requests two protected resources on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 254,
          "start": 789.72,
          "end": 792.7,
          "en": "So two protected API routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 255,
          "start": 792.7,
          "end": 795.31,
          "en": "And for example, if you wanna change our password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 256,
          "start": 795.31,
          "end": 798.52,
          "en": "we don't just send the old and the new password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 257,
          "start": 798.52,
          "end": 803.35,
          "en": "but we also include that token in the outgoing request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 258,
          "start": 803.35,
          "end": 807.14,
          "en": "And that token then is validated by the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 259,
          "start": 807.14,
          "end": 808.88,
          "en": "which basically checks...",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 260,
          "start": 808.88,
          "end": 813.44,
          "en": "Okay. If I would use my signing key which only I know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 261,
          "start": 813.44,
          "end": 816.83,
          "en": "would I be able to generate this token?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 262,
          "start": 816.83,
          "end": 818.16,
          "en": "And if the answer is, yes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 263,
          "start": 818.16,
          "end": 819.9,
          "en": "The server knows that it's valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 264,
          "start": 819.9,
          "end": 821.06,
          "en": "If the answer is no.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 265,
          "start": 821.06,
          "end": 824.21,
          "en": "It's invalid and access is denied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 266,
          "start": 824.21,
          "end": 827.2,
          "en": "So that's why we can't just generate a token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 267,
          "start": 827.2,
          "end": 828.73,
          "en": "without knowing the key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 268,
          "start": 828.73,
          "end": 831,
          "en": "We can't generate a token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 269,
          "start": 831,
          "end": 832.81,
          "en": "but it would be an invalid one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 270,
          "start": 832.81,
          "end": 835.203,
          "en": "And that's why this is a secure mechanism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 271,
          "start": 836.14,
          "end": 837.76,
          "en": "Okay. That was a lot of talking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 272,
